[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676063113","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103141#issuecomment-2676063113","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103141","id":2676063113,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fgXuJ","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-22T07:06:17Z","updated_at":"2025-02-22T07:06:17Z","body":"I'm not sure if this is the direction we want to take the compatibility renderer. We intentionally chose to use an approximation to keep the renderer as efficient as possible. We potentially do the sRGB->linear conversion several times per pixel, so avoiding expensive operations is very useful. \r\n\r\nIt's nice to make the color representation slightly more accurate for niche use cases, but the reality is that 99% of users will never noticed the difference. Should those users pay the cost of this change?\r\n\r\nI guess we should evaluate the real cost of this change before making a decision. When writing this code I remember there being a measurable difference in performance from using the approximation, but the code has become more complex since then so the actual impact may be smaller than it was before. In which case my objection might not be warranted. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676063113/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676089582","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103141#issuecomment-2676089582","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103141","id":2676089582,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fgeLu","user":{"login":"celyk","id":50609684,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNjA5Njg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50609684?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk","html_url":"https://github.com/celyk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-22T08:26:32Z","updated_at":"2025-02-22T08:26:32Z","body":"I can accept another solution for my issue. When rendering textures to Viewports I always use `render_mode unshaded;` and linear tone mapping. Perhaps you can remove the sRGB conversions in that case?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676089582/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676091108","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103141#issuecomment-2676091108","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103141","id":2676091108,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fgejk","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-22T08:31:38Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T03:10:38Z","body":"> I can accept another solution for my issue. When rendering textures to Viewports I always use `render_mode unshaded;` and linear tone mapping. Perhaps you can remove the sRGB conversions in that case?\r\n\r\nThat could work. I'd need to check. Right now the flow is:\r\n1. User's fragment shader runs (all in sRGB)\r\n2. Convert input colors to linear (ALBEDO, EMISSION, etc.)\r\n3. Calculate lighting in linear space \r\n4. Convert final color to sRGB\r\n\r\nIf using unshaded, we should be able to avoid any conversions altogether (unless I am forgetting something)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676091108/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676102766","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103141#issuecomment-2676102766","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103141","id":2676102766,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fghZu","user":{"login":"BakeMyCake","id":25646269,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjQ2MjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25646269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BakeMyCake","html_url":"https://github.com/BakeMyCake","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BakeMyCake/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BakeMyCake/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BakeMyCake/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BakeMyCake/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BakeMyCake/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BakeMyCake/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BakeMyCake/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BakeMyCake/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BakeMyCake/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-22T08:47:09Z","updated_at":"2025-02-22T08:47:09Z","body":"> I'm not sure if this is the direction we want to take the compatibility renderer. We intentionally chose to use an approximation to keep the renderer as efficient as possible. We potentially do the sRGB->linear conversion several times per pixel, so avoiding expensive operations is very useful.\r\n> \r\n> It's nice to make the color representation slightly more accurate for niche use cases, but the reality is that 99% of users will never noticed the difference. Should those users pay the cost of this change?\r\n> \r\n> I guess we should evaluate the real cost of this change before making a decision. When writing this code I remember there being a measurable difference in performance from using the approximation, but the code has become more complex since then so the actual impact may be smaller than it was before. In which case my objection might not be warranted.\r\n\r\nAs someone impacted by this issue, I would propose a middle ground:\r\nIf this change is not acceptable for performance reasons, can we have an option to enable the correct but costly color calculation path? That way, you can retain the performance benefits of cheap color calculation, and keep it as default behavior, but also give a way out for people who need color correctness and are willing to carry the responsibility of sacrificed performance.\r\n\r\nIf there is already a workaround for this, I would retract my proposal, but I am not aware of one","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676102766/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676116504","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103141#issuecomment-2676116504","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103141","id":2676116504,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fgkwY","user":{"login":"precup","id":709680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTY4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/709680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup","html_url":"https://github.com/precup","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-22T09:22:09Z","updated_at":"2025-02-22T09:22:09Z","body":"If it's unshaded and has a linear tonemapper it looks like the only things being done to it while it's linear are the fog mix and exposure multiplication.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676116504/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2712449748","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103141#issuecomment-2712449748","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103141","id":2712449748,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hrLLU","user":{"login":"celyk","id":50609684,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNjA5Njg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50609684?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk","html_url":"https://github.com/celyk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celyk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T03:09:16Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T07:34:04Z","body":"linear_to_srgb() is not accurate enough near 0. My tolerance is ±0.5/255 to ensure that RGB8 values will be unaltered.\r\n\r\nThe linear portion of the curve is neglected, because for linear_to_srgb() it only matters in [0, 0.0031308]. This seems like an insignificant interval, but it corresponds to a greater interval of [0, 0.04045] on the inverse. I'm noticing that the first few values are still being changed by the functions, even though they're meant to cancel out. Only the very darkest colors are affected, which is why it was hard to notice before. Correcting linear_to_srgb() in that interval fixes it.\r\n\r\nShadertoy demo:\r\nhttps://www.shadertoy.com/view/wc2SRW","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2712449748/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4402648235","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103141#issuecomment-4402648235","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103141","id":4402648235,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBmsUqw","user":{"login":"wagnerfs","id":106078,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjA3OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106078?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs","html_url":"https://github.com/wagnerfs","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-08T01:49:51Z","updated_at":"2026-05-08T01:49:51Z","body":"I kinda wonder, don't we already have a proper linear to srgb conversion when getting screen texture in canvas items? Because the colors seem perfectly fine there but messed up when fetching in 3D. 🤔","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4402648235/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4407389409","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103141#issuecomment-4407389409","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103141","id":4407389409,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBrNs4Q","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.